  "question": {
    "text": "Electrons with de-Broglie wavelength $\\lambda$ fall on the target in an X-ray tube. The cut-off wavelength of the emitted X-rays is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "TMWCf",
      "text": "\n$\\lambda_0=\\frac{2 m c \\lambda^2}{h}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "NFxgp",
      "text": "\n$\\lambda_0=\\frac{2 h}{m c}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "21MUe",
      "text": "\n$\\lambda_0=\\frac{2 m^2 c^2 \\lambda^3}{h^2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bbiKS",
      "text": "\n$\\lambda_0=\\lambda$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Momentum of striking electrons, $p=\\frac{h}{\\lambda}$\n$\\therefore$ Kinetic energy of striking electrons, $K=\\frac{p^2}{2 m}=\\frac{h^2}{2 m \\lambda^2}$\nThis is also, maximum energy of $X$-ray photons.\nTherefore, $\\quad \\frac{h c}{\\lambda_0}=\\frac{h^2}{2 m \\lambda^2}$ or $\\lambda_0=\\frac{2 m \\lambda^2 c}{h}$\n$\\therefore$ Correct option is (a).",
    "image": null
  },
